# `sum += text.length; sum += holder.extra; sum += text.length`, nothing proven of either. The read of `extra` may run a getter. It cannot end the proof that the text is a string, and still the stretch of the guess ends in front of it:
# what goes on over such a read is the stretch between the read of a method and its call, `text.charCodeAt(holder.at)`, and the index says where the call stands. A finder that goes on to the end of the block for every guess looks at
# each place of the block once for each guess: "texts that move up one place in every turn of a loop" of test/aot/build-scaling/shapes.ts: 3.6 G > 64.5 G at 4,000 texts. So the text is tested once in front of the read and once behind it.
